Package: grainPlan
Title: Grain-Specific Decision Orchestration on Top of Decision Theory
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Max",
           family = "Moldovan",
           email = "max.moldovan@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: Turns an orchestra inference result into an actionable
    grain-production plan. It is a thin grain-semantics layer on top of the
    'decideR' decision engine: it reuses that engine, its grade-band loss
    library, its manifest-native pipeline tail, and its grounding firewall,
    and adds the grain economics those decisions kept re-deriving. Named grain
    decisions price a nitrogen rate by expected profit, rank a variety from a
    multi-environment trial under downside-aware merit, and target a quality
    grade against a delivery standard. A reusable, documented grain value
    library supplies wheat protein bands, barley malting premiums, and
    nitrogen-rate economics built from published price structures. A season
    plan composes several grain decisions into one provenance-carrying object
    whose grounding is the worst case across its decisions, so a plan resting
    on any unverified input abstains rather than asserting a confident wrong
    recommendation.
